Subject: Size the frame's control stack from the emitted IR, not the stack bytecode

What this does
  Size the frame's control stack from the emitted IR, not the stack bytecode.

Why we need it
  The frame allocates `sizeof(JSRegCtl) * regvm_ctl_count`, where the liveness cap refused those functions first; the baseline tier exposed it.

What it adds
  The count is derived from the emitted IR, where the lowering has already turned the sentinel drop into `ROP_sentinel_drop`, so a push and its matching pop balance. `regvm_ctl_delta_rop` gives the per-register-instruction effect -- the four pushes `ROP_catch_enter`/`ROP_finally_enter`/`ROP_iter_start`/`ROP_for_await_of_start` and the four pops `ROP_finally_leave`/`ROP_nip_catch`/`ROP_iter_close`/`ROP_sentinel_drop` -- and `regvm_ctl_bound` sums it per source pc and runs the same block dataflow as before, with one correction: a `catch` block's handler edge enters with the unwinder having already popped the entry the `catch` pushed, so the handler starts one below the fall-through.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
